      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "docs: add Features capability explorer",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Reframe the Features index around reusable capabilities rather than providers or command syntax.\n- Replace the long generated Markdown list with a polished, responsive capability explorer on `/features/`.\n- Add a strong product-oriented hero, a Lease → Sync → Run → Prove flow, live search, category filters, result counts, and linked capability cards.\n- Keep provider discovery in the canonical Provider Reference and command syntax in the Command Reference.\n- Preserve every existing feature document and URL; the enhancement runs after the normal docs build and only transforms the Features landing page.\n\n## Why\n\nThe docs now give Providers a first-class section, but the Features landing page still behaved like a dense Markdown inventory and duplicated adjacent information architecture. It was technically complete but difficult to scan, did not communicate the product workflow, and made dozens of capability guides feel flat and undifferentiated.\n\nThis change gives `/features/` one clear job: help a reader understand what Crabbox can do and quickly find the relevant capability contract.\n\n## UX and accessibility\n\n- Responsive three-, two-, and one-column card layouts.\n- Searchable capability titles and descriptions.\n- Filter pills for each capability area, with pressed state and live result counts.\n- Keyboard-friendly native links, buttons, labels, and search input.\n- Escape clears an active search.\n- Empty-result status is announced and category sections hide only when they have no visible cards.\n- Existing light/dark theme variables and reduced-motion behavior remain authoritative.\n- Provider and command CTAs create an explicit handoff to the correct top-level section.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe shared Markdown renderer remains unchanged. `scripts/enhance-docs-site.mjs` deterministically post-processes only `dist/docs-site/features/index.html` after the normal build. This isolates the richer landing-page treatment from all other documentation pages and avoids committing generated output.\n\nThe Pages workflow and `scripts/check-docs.sh` both run the enhancement, so CI validates the same output that is deployed.\n\n## Visual proof\n\nThe `Docs UI Proof / Render visual proof` check builds the exact generated docs output from the PR head, runs the enhancer and regression tests, and renders browser screenshots with pinned Playwright/Chromium.\n\nIts downloadable artifact is named `features-ui-proof-<head-sha>` and contains:\n\n- `features-desktop-light.png` — full desktop layout in light mode.\n- `features-desktop-dark.png` — full desktop layout using the dark color scheme.\n- `features-mobile.png` — full responsive mobile layout using an iPhone viewport.\n- `SHA256SUMS` — digests binding each proof image to the workflow artifact.\n\nThe proof job also fails unless the generated page contains the capability explorer, product hero, provider handoff, and command-reference handoff. This makes the evidence reproducible rather than a manually edited screenshot.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node --check scripts/enhance-docs-site.mjs`\n- `node --test scripts/enhance-docs-site.test.mjs`\n- Enhancer regression coverage verifies the hero, search/filter surface, capability-card generation, TOC/pager removal, idempotence, and no-op behavior for unrelated pages.\n- `Docs UI Proof / Render visual proof` publishes desktop light, desktop dark, and mobile screenshots from the exact built PR output.\n- Branch is based directly on upstream `main` (`6da7760693a820c53434b4774077f526d362c136`) with no unrelated files.\n\nGenerated site output remains uncommitted.",
